# .dockerignore - at the REPOSITORY ROOT, because the build context is the repository root.
#
# This file is the single biggest influence on build speed. Without it the whole of node_modules and
# .next is uploaded to the daemon as build context on every build, which on this project is hundreds
# of megabytes to send before a single layer is considered.

# Dependencies and build output are rebuilt in the image, never copied into it.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/out
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Version control and local tool state.
.git
.gitattributes
**/.DS_Store
**/.idea
**/.vscode
**/coverage
**/.vitest

# Secrets never enter an image. The example file is the only one that travels.
scaffold/.env
scaffold/.env.*
!scaffold/.env.example

# Generated data. Produced inside the container by gen:programs and gen:roster, deterministically,
# so copying a host's copy in would only be a way for the two to disagree.
data/programs
data/roster
data/history

# Documentation, the kit's own docs, and the brain. None of it is served.
docs
kit-docs
*.md
!scaffold/README.md

# ...with one exception, which is not documentation at all. seed-framework.mjs re-parses
# kit-docs/03_COMPETENCY_FRAMEWORK.md and byte-matches all 73 observable behaviours against it
# before it will write a single row: the document is the AUTHORITY and the JSON seed is the copy.
# Excluding it made `seed:framework` the first step of the instance build to fail in a container,
# on a path that reads like a docs file nobody could need.
!kit-docs/03_COMPETENCY_FRAMEWORK.md
